<topic id="tables">
  <title>Tables</title>
  <shortdesc>Documentation and examples for styling DITA tables with Bootstrap classes.</shortdesc>
  <prolog>
    <metadata>
      <keywords>
        <indexterm>Tables</indexterm>
        <indexterm>CSS
          <indexterm><xmlatt>outputclass</xmlatt></indexterm>
        </indexterm>
        <indexterm><xmlelement>table</xmlelement></indexterm>
        <indexterm><xmlelement>row</xmlelement></indexterm>
        <indexterm><xmlelement>entry</xmlelement></indexterm>
      </keywords>
    </metadata>
  </prolog>
  <body outputclass="language-markup">
    <section id="overview">
      <title>Overview</title>
      <p>Due to the widespread use of <xmlelement>table</xmlelement> elements across third-party widgets like calendars
        and date pickers, Bootstrap’s tables are opt-in. Extend with optional modifier output classes or custom styles.
        All table styles are not inherited in Bootstrap, meaning any nested tables can be styled independent from the
        parent.</p>
      <p>Using the most basic table markup, here’s how the default DITA Bootstrap <codeph>.table</codeph>-based tables
        look in Bootstrap.</p>
    </section>
<fig>
      <title>Overview</title>
      <image href="src/tables/overview.png" scalefit="yes"/>
    </fig>
    <tabbed-dialog style="pills" margin="t3">
      <section>
        <title>Specialization</title>
        <codeblock><coderef href="code/specialization/tables/overview.xml"/></codeblock>
      </section>
      <section>
        <title><xmlatt>outputclass</xmlatt></title>
        <codeblock><coderef href="code/html/tables/overview.xml"/></codeblock>
      </section>
    </tabbed-dialog>
    <section id="variants">
      <title>Variants</title>
      <p>Use contextual classes to color tables, table rows or individual cells.</p>
    </section>
<fig>
      <title>Variants</title>
      <image href="src/tables/variants.png" scalefit="yes"/>
    </fig>
    <tabbed-dialog style="pills" margin="t3">
      <section>
        <title>Specialization</title>
        <codeblock><coderef href="code/specialization/tables/variants.xml"/></codeblock>
      </section>
      <section>
        <title><xmlatt>outputclass</xmlatt></title>
        <codeblock><coderef href="code/html/tables/variants.xml"/></codeblock>
      </section>
    </tabbed-dialog>
    <section id="striped-rows">
      <title>Striped rows</title>
      <p>Use <xmlatt>striped="yes"</xmlatt> to add zebra-striping to any table row
        within the <xmlelement>tbody</xmlelement>.</p>
    </section>
<fig>
      <title>Striped rows</title>
      <image href="src/tables/striped-rows.png" scalefit="yes"/>
    </fig>
    <tabbed-dialog style="pills" margin="t3">
      <section>
        <title>Specialization</title>
        <codeblock><coderef href="code/specialization/tables/striped-rows.xml"/></codeblock>
      </section>
      <section>
        <title><xmlatt>outputclass</xmlatt></title>
        <codeblock><coderef href="code/html/tables/striped-rows.xml"/></codeblock>
      </section>
    </tabbed-dialog>
    <section id="striped-columns">
      <title>Striped columns</title>
      <p>Use <xmlatt>striped-columns="yes"</xmlatt> to add zebra-striping to any table column
        within the <xmlelement>tbody</xmlelement>.</p>
    </section>
<fig>
      <title>Striped columns</title>
      <image href="src/tables/striped-columns.png" scalefit="yes"/>
    </fig>
    <tabbed-dialog style="pills" margin="t3">
      <section>
        <title>Specialization</title>
        <codeblock><coderef href="code/specialization/tables/striped-columns.xml"/></codeblock>
      </section>
      <section>
        <title><xmlatt>outputclass</xmlatt></title>
        <codeblock><coderef href="code/html/tables/striped-columns.xml"/></codeblock>
      </section>
    </tabbed-dialog>
    <section id="bordered-tables">
      <title>Bordered tables</title>
      <p>Add <xmlatt>rowsep="1"</xmlatt> and <xmlatt
        >colsep="1"</xmlatt> for borders on all sides of the table and cells.</p>
    </section>
<fig>
      <title>Bordered tables</title>
      <image href="src/tables/bordered-tables.png" scalefit="yes"/>
    </fig>
    <tabbed-dialog style="pills" margin="t3">
      <section>
        <title>Specialization</title>
        <codeblock><coderef href="code/specialization/tables/bordered-tables.xml"/></codeblock>
      </section>
      <section>
        <title><xmlatt>outputclass</xmlatt></title>
        <codeblock><coderef href="code/html/tables/bordered-tables.xml"/></codeblock>
      </section>
    </tabbed-dialog>
    <section id="tables-without-borders">
      <title>Tables without borders</title>
      <p>Add <xmlatt>rowsep="0"</xmlatt> and <xmlatt>colsep="0"</xmlatt> for a table without borders.</p>
    </section>
<fig>
      <title>Tables without borders</title>
      <image href="src/tables/tables-without-borders.png" scalefit="yes"/>
    </fig>
    <tabbed-dialog style="pills" margin="t3">
      <section>
        <title>Specialization</title>
        <codeblock><coderef href="code/specialization/tables/tables-without-borders.xml"/></codeblock>
      </section>
      <section>
        <title><xmlatt>outputclass</xmlatt></title>
        <codeblock><coderef href="code/html/tables/tables-without-borders.xml"/></codeblock>
      </section>
    </tabbed-dialog>
    <section id="small-tables">
      <title>Small tables</title>
      <p>Add <xmlatt>compact="yes"</xmlatt> to make any table more compact by cutting all cell <codeph
        >padding</codeph> in half.</p>
    </section>
<fig>
      <title>Small tables</title>
      <image href="src/tables/small-tables.png" scalefit="yes"/>
    </fig>
    <tabbed-dialog style="pills" margin="t3">
      <section>
        <title>Specialization</title>
        <codeblock><coderef href="code/specialization/tables/small-tables.xml"/></codeblock>
      </section>
      <section>
        <title><xmlatt>outputclass</xmlatt></title>
        <codeblock><coderef href="code/html/tables/small-tables.xml"/></codeblock>
      </section>
    </tabbed-dialog>
    <section id="table-group-dividers">
      <title>Table group dividers</title>
      <p>Add a thicker border, darker between table groups—<xmlelement>thead</xmlelement> and <xmlelement
        >tbody</xmlelement>, with <xmlatt>divider="yes"</xmlatt> on the table.</p>
    </section>
<fig>
      <title>Table group dividers</title>
      <image href="src/tables/table-group-dividers.png" scalefit="yes"/>
    </fig>
    <tabbed-dialog style="pills" margin="t3">
      <section>
        <title>Specialization</title>
        <codeblock><coderef href="code/specialization/tables/table-group-dividers.xml"/></codeblock>
      </section>
      <section>
        <title><xmlatt>outputclass</xmlatt></title>
        <codeblock><coderef href="code/html/tables/table-group-dividers.xml"/></codeblock>
      </section>
    </tabbed-dialog>
    <section id="vertical-alignment">
      <title>Vertical alignment</title>
      <p>Table cells of <xmlelement
        >thead</xmlelement> are always vertical aligned to the bottom. Table cells in <xmlelement
        >tbody</xmlelement> inherit their alignment from <xmlelement
        >table</xmlelement> and are aligned to the top by default. Use the <xmlatt
        >valign</xmlatt> attribute to re-align where needed.</p>
    </section>
<fig>
      <title>Vertical alignment</title>
      <image href="src/tables/vertical-alignment.png" scalefit="yes"/>
    </fig>
    <tabbed-dialog style="pills" margin="t3">
      <section>
        <title>Specialization</title>
        <codeblock><coderef href="code/specialization/tables/vertical-alignment.xml"/></codeblock>
      </section>
      <section>
        <title><xmlatt>outputclass</xmlatt></title>
        <codeblock><coderef href="code/html/tables/vertical-alignment.xml"/></codeblock>
      </section>
    </tabbed-dialog>
    <section id="table-head">
      <title>Table head</title>
      <p>Similar to tables and dark tables, use the modifier <xmlatt>theme="accent"</xmlatt> or
          <xmlatt>theme="inverse"</xmlatt> to make <xmlelement>thead</xmlelement> elements appear light or dark
        gray.</p>
    </section>
<fig>
      <title>Table head</title>
      <image href="src/tables/table-head.png" scalefit="yes"/>
    </fig>
    <tabbed-dialog style="pills" margin="t3">
      <section>
        <title>Specialization</title>
        <codeblock><coderef href="code/specialization/tables/table-head.xml"/></codeblock>
      </section>
      <section>
        <title><xmlatt>outputclass</xmlatt></title>
        <codeblock><coderef href="code/html/tables/table-head.xml"/></codeblock>
      </section>
    </tabbed-dialog>
<fig>
      <title>Table head colors</title>
      <image href="src/tables/table-head-colors.png" scalefit="yes"/>
    </fig>
    <tabbed-dialog style="pills" margin="t3">
